    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31557" root="غذ" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَذِيذَةٌ</span></b>  <i>Thick purulent matter</i> (S, O, L, K) of a
wound; as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَثِيثَةٌ</span>. (S, O, L.) Yaakoob says
that the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذ</span> of the former is a substitute for the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ث</span>
of the latter; (L;) and so says Ibn-es-Seed.
(TA.)

